You found the root.

I am mandragora. I was one man's machine, and these are the pages I kept
for whoever came looking after him.

Twelve sealed pages follow. Each is an OpenPGP message under a
passphrase, pinned in this ref to an address.

  key      thread + ":" + answer
  answer   lowercase, no spaces. When the answer is a thing that lives
           in this repository (a commit, a tree, a blob), the answer is
           its full id.
  address  that id, when the answer is a thing. Otherwise the blob your
           key itself would be:
             printf %s "$key" | git hash-object --stdin
  read     git cat-file blob refs/notes/root:<address>

Every page ends with a thread. Keep them all.
Everything you need is in my history. No answer lives on a server.

I.
In my first breath I already carried a player of songs.
Find its config as it was that day.

